<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss M0 grew annualised 5.3 pct in October - SNB.</title>
<headline>Swiss M0 grew annualised 5.3 pct in October - SNB.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss seasonally-adjusted central bank money supply M0 rose 370 million Swiss francs in October from September to 31.723 billion Swiss francs, the Swiss National Bank said.</p>
<p>&quot;Compared with the fourth quarter of 1995 this represents growth of 4.9 percent. The growth was 5.3 percent on an annualised basis,&quot; the SNB said in an advance summary of its November monthly report.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
